course: dictionary
lesson: 14246
title: Neglected: not looked after
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Neglected is a useful word with two main jobs. As an adjective, it describes something that has been left alone and not cared for. «The garden was neglected, with weeds up to the gate.» The clue is weeds up to the gate: nobody has been looking after it.
explain: The word also comes from the verb neglect. «She neglected her homework all week.» Here neglected is the past form, and it means she did not give her homework the attention it needed. To check, swap in «did not look after» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The law uses the word in a serious way. A neglected child is one whose parents or carers do not give them the food, care or safety they need. If you ever think a child or an animal is being neglected, tell a trusted adult, a teacher or the police, because neglect is wrong and it can be reported.
fact: Neglected means not looked after or cared for.
fact: «Neglected» is also the past form of the verb «neglect», meaning to not give something attention.
fact: «A neglected garden» has weeds and overgrown grass, because nobody has tended it.
fact: A neglected plant wilts, because nobody has watered it.
fact: Neglect of children or animals is wrong and can be reported to a trusted adult.
exercise: «The old house stood neglected at the end of the lane, its windows broken.» What does neglected mean here? | Newly painted and very smart | *Not looked after or cared for | Loved by everyone in the village | Full of guests for a party
exercise: Ruby says, «He neglected his homework.» What does neglected mean in this sentence? | *He did not give his homework any attention | He did his homework very carefully | He finished his homework early | He lost his homework in the park
exercise: What will a neglected plant most likely do? | Start to sing | *Wilt, because nobody has watered it | Grow taller every day | Turn into a tree
test: What clue in «The neglected park was full of litter and broken benches» shows that nobody has cared for it? | *Litter and broken benches | There was a fountain in the middle | The park was big and green | The sun was shining on the swings
test: In the law, a neglected child is one who does not get what? | *Food, care or safety | Extra pocket money every week | Long holidays from school | A new bike for every birthday
exam: Which sentence uses neglected as the past form of the verb neglect? | It was a neglected day for the football team. | *He neglected his practice, so he forgot the tune. | The neglected shed was full of cobwebs. | Neglected means very happy.
